/AP <<
/N 42 0 R
>>
/DS (font: Helvetica,sans-serif 12.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )
/F 4
/FT /Tx
/Ff 33558528
/MK <<
>>
/P 37 0 R
/RV (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xfa:APIVersion="Acroform:2.7.0.0" xfa:spec="2.1" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">Problem:<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160; </span>Newer pilots who do not understand what an FAA medical certificate requires, how to obtain one, and the steps/hacks to get get through the process successfully.</p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">Sub problems:<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160; </span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">where do they obtain accurate information,<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">what information needs to be disclosed on their medical,<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">what happens if they disclose,<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">how do they easily find the information that will help them,<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">what happens if the physician they see \(Aviation Medical Examiner\) is unable to give them a medical certificate</p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">what do all those medical words mean?<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160; </span></p></body>)
/Rect [70.795 509.547 609.624 646.155]
/Subtype /Widget
/T (Text1)
/Type /Annot
/V <>
>>
endobj
12 0 obj
<<
/AP <<
/N 43 0 R
>>
/DS (font: Helvetica,sans-serif 12.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )
/F 4
/FT /Tx
/Ff 33558528
/MK <<
>>
/P 37 0 R
/RV (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xfa:APIVersion="Acroform:2.7.0.0" xfa:spec="2.1" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">Create a web platform/website/page \(must be within FAA acceptable framework\) that is easy for new pilots to find.</p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">Make it a page they want to use and easy to navigate.</p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">Fill it with information that makes sense to to a new pilot.</p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">With correct medical content \(provided\), develop tools to help new pilots obtain correct answers to their medical questions.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;&#160; </span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">Make sure pilots know they should first get healthy, take care of their health, see their physicians if they do have a medical concern, understand medical concerns with being a pilot, then work on their medical certificate.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p></body>)
/Rect [70.7888 360.419 610.128 496.699]
/Subtype /Widget
/T (Text2)
/Type /Annot
/V <>
>>
endobj
13 0 obj
<<
/AP <<
/N 44 0 R
>>
/DS (font: Helvetica,sans-serif 12.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )
/F 4
/FT /Tx
/Ff 33558528
/MK <<
>>
/P 37 0 R
/RV (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xfa:APIVersion="Acroform:2.7.0.0" xfa:spec="2.1" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">Increase in pilot medical certificate applications over past 2 years.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160; </span>They often have medical conditions including mental health issues and think their pilot career is over before it starts.</p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">Solutions:<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160; </span>Educate pilots on where to find accurate information on what they need to provide and<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160; </span>what to expect in the process.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160; </span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">Design specs: Continue the work that occurred in the fall 2025 and spring 2026 semesters with Dr. Abdulhak's student team.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160; </span>The previous student teams prototyped many different concepts including AI assisted searches, interactive graphics, and JSON files to demonstrate the art of possible with AI along with the accuracy of results and presented them to FAA CAMI leadership.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160; </span>The concepts are ready for more detailed work and potential integration with the FAA Office of Communication.</p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12pt">Stakeholder requirements:<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160; </span>Content should be accurate, easy to find, easy to understand and encouraging.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">&#160;&#160; </span></p></body>)
/Rect [70.0212 187.779 609.974 334.734]
/Subtype /Widget
/T (Text3)
/Type /Annot
/V <>
>>
endobj
